-- title:
--   Reading admissible level-M' functions gives a κ_A-embedding
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is the algebraic closure of $\mathbb Q$, and for a valuation subring $B$ the symbol $\kappa_B$ denotes its residue field. For a field $L$, `jqModC L` is the Laurent series $\mathsf q^{-1}\cdot(\text{the integral }j\text{-numerator})$ over $L$, `qExpand L d` is the substitution $\mathsf q \mapsto \mathsf q^{d}$, `modularFunctionFieldC L N` $= L(j(\mathsf q), j(\mathsf q^{N}))$ and `modularFunctionFieldFullC L N` $= L\bigl(j(\mathsf q^{d}) : d \mid N\bigr)$; over $\mathbb Q$, `modularFunctionFieldFull N` is the subfield of $\mathbb Q((\mathsf q))$ generated by the $j(\mathsf q^{d})$ with $d \mid N$, and `modularFunctionFieldBar N` is the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((\mathsf q))$ generated over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ by the coefficientwise image of that field.
--
--   **Global data.** A prime $q$ with $5 \le q$ (`hq`); a nonzero $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$ (`hqM'`); a valuation subring $A \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$ (`hA`). A finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ_A M'` over $\kappa_A$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' κ_A` (`hW`), namely those places $w$ that are $\kappa_A$-rational, satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and whose value at the generator `jGeomGen` lies in `ssJSet q κ_A`; a chosen element $s$ of $W$. An inclusion `hle` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` into `fieldBar q M'`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the $X_H$-function field of level $q^{2}M'$ with $H =$ `levelH q M'` the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^{2}M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$.
--
--   **The constant reduction $R_0$.** A `ConstantReduction` datum for $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC κ_A M'`: a valuation subring `R₀.integers` of the former, a surjective ring homomorphism `R₀.residue` onto the latter whose kernel is the maximal ideal of `R₀.integers`, a map `R₀.placeMap` on places, together with the axioms that a constant $x \in \overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in `R₀.integers` exactly when $x \in A$, that on constants the residue is the residue map of $A$, that every nonzero element becomes a nonzero residue after scaling by a suitable constant, that `placeMap` preserves degrees, and that `placeMap` pushes the divisor of an element with nonzero residue to the divisor of that residue. The hypothesis `hR₀` is a coefficientwise-reduction compatibility: for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((\mathsf q))$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element lies in `R₀.integers` and its residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa_A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   **Local data over a subfield $k_0$.** An intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and an element $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lying in $A$ (`hπ`). Write $A_0 :=$ `A.comap (algebraMap k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))`, the valuation subring $A \cap k_0$ of $k_0$. It is assumed that $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), that $A_0$ is Henselian local (`hhens`), that $\kappa_{A_0}$ is algebraically closed (`hres`), and (`hκ`) that every $a \in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$.
--
--   **Auxiliary prime and the field $K$.** A prime $\ell'$ with $\ell' \ne q$, $3 \le \ell'$ and $\ell' \nmid M'$; an element $\xi \in k_0$ which is a primitive $(q\ell')$-th root of unity (`hξ`), normalised by `hιξ`: there is a ring homomorphism $\iota : k_0 \to \mathbb C$ with $\iota(\xi) = \exp(2\pi i/(q\ell'))$. An intermediate field $K$ of $k_0((\mathsf q))/k_0$ equal (`hK`) to the $k_0$-base change of `xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ')^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ') M')`, the level being $(q\ell')^{2}M'$ and the subgroup being the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/(q\ell')^{2}M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q\ell')^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell'$; $K$ is regarded as an $A_0$-algebra compatibly with $k_0$. An element $j \in K$, assumed nonzero, whose image in $k_0((\mathsf q))$ is the coefficientwise image of `jq` (`hj`). Write $C_j :=$ `chartAlgFin A₀ K j`, the $A_0$-subalgebra of $K$ of elements integral over $A_0[j]$, and `jChartFin` for $j$ viewed in $C_j$.
--
--   **Functoriality and group-law hypotheses.** `hℓ`: for every commutative $A_0$-algebra $T$, Weierstrass curve $W$ over $T$, variable change $C$ and `LevelPData` $D$, if $D$ is a level-$\ell'$ structure on $W$ then `D.variableChange C` is one on $C \bullet W$. `hM`: the analogous equivariance of `IsGamma0PowAt` under `kernelVariableChangeDeg`. A family of group laws $\mathcal G$ on the projective models of Weierstrass curves over $A_0$-algebras, assumed chord-and-tangent (`h𝒢`: each group law is computed by a points-evaluation equivalence) and with the origin as identity (`h𝒢O`). A `LevelTransport` $\mathcal T$ for $\mathcal G$ and $q$ (transport of raw Drinfeld pairs along algebra maps and variable changes, preserving the Drinfeld-basis condition), assumed to be a section transport (`h𝒯`). `hVC` and `hCO`: for every $A_0$-algebra $T$ and projective Weierstrass curve over $T$, existence of graded ring homomorphisms of projective-model rings, with the required containment of irrelevant ideals, realising respectively a given variable change (`IsVariableChangeHom`) and a given coefficient homomorphism (`IsCoefficientHom`).
--
--   **The moduli package and the Tate point.** Let $\mathcal R :=$ `rigidDataPow A₀ ℓ' M' q hℓ hM 𝒢 𝒯`, the rigid Weierstrass data whose raw objects over an $A_0$-algebra $T$ consist of a Weierstrass curve with unit discriminant together with level data of three kinds: a family of $\Gamma_0(p^{v_p(M')})$-kernel polynomials indexed by the prime factors $p$ of $M'$, a level-$\ell'$ structure (`LevelPData`), and a raw Drinfeld pair forming a $q$-basis for $\mathcal G$; points over $T$ are such raw objects modulo variable change, with `jOf` the $j$-invariant. The data consist of: an absolute moduli package $P_0$ for $\mathcal R$, i.e. an $A_0$-algebra $B_0$ with a universal point representing the functor of points; a point $x_0$ of $\mathcal R$ over $K$ whose $j$-invariant has image `jqNModC k₀ (q*ℓ')`, that is $j(\mathsf q^{q\ell'})$, in $k_0((\mathsf q))$ (`hx₀`); an $A_0$-algebra homomorphism `clC` from $B_0$ to $C_j$ which, composed with $C_j \subseteq K$, is the classifying map `P₀.classify x₀` of $x_0$ (`hclC`).
--
--   The hypothesis `hμ` identifies $x_0$ with a Tate point at the cusp: there are a variable change $C$ over $k_0((\mathsf q))$ and a raw object $r$ of $\mathcal R$ over $K$ such that (i) the class of $r$ is $x_0$; (ii) writing $(x_\infty, y_\infty) =$ `cuspPoint k₀ (q*ℓ') ξ ![1,0]` for the toric point attached to $\xi$, one has $C.u\,(2x_\infty + 1/6) = 2y_\infty + x_\infty$, $C.r = -1/12$, $C.s = -1/2$, $C.t = 1/24$; (iii) the curve of $r$, base changed to $k_0((\mathsf q))$, is $C \bullet$ `tateBase k₀ (q*ℓ')`; (iv) for every prime factor $p$ of $M'$, every field $F'$ with a ring homomorphism $f : k_0 \to F'$ and every primitive $p^{v_p(M')}$-th root of unity $\zeta \in F'$, the image of the $p$-component $r.\mathrm{level}.1\,p$ in $F'((\mathsf q))$ is the `kernelVariableChangeDeg` transform, along $C$ mapped by $f$ and in degree `gamma0PowDeg p (M'.factorization p)`, of $\prod_a (X - x(\mathrm{toricPoint}\ F'\,(q\ell')\,\zeta^{a}))$, the product over $1 \le a \le p^{v_p(M')}/2$ with $p \nmid a$; (v) the image of the level-$\ell'$ component $r.\mathrm{level}.2.1$ is `cuspData k₀ (q*ℓ') ξ ![q,0] ![0,-q]` transformed by $C$; (vi) there are $P_x, P_y, Q_x, Q_y \in K$ whose images in $k_0((\mathsf q))$ are the four coordinates of `cuspData k₀ (q*ℓ') ξ ![ℓ',0] ![0,-ℓ']` transformed by $C$, and the two sections of the Drinfeld component $r.\mathrm{level}.2.2$ pass through $(P_x,P_y)$ and $(Q_x,Q_y)$ in the sense of `IsSectionThrough`.
--
--   **Residue-field comparison.** A ring homomorphism $\theta : \kappa_{A_0} \to \kappa_A$ compatible with the two residue maps along $A_0 \subseteq A$ (`hθ`).
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every maximal ideal $y$ of $C_j$, every $A_0$-algebra homomorphism $\psi : C_j \to \kappa_{A_0}$ whose vanishing locus is exactly $y$ (that is, $\psi c = 0$ if and only if $c \in y$), and every admissible block consisting of a field $\Omega$ that is a $\kappa_A$-algebra, a place $V$ of $\Omega$ over $\kappa_A$ (a proper valuation subring $\mathcal O_V$ of $\Omega$ containing the image of $\kappa_A$, whose ideals are principal), a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{res} : \kappa(V) \to \kappa_A$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho : C_j \to \mathcal O_V$ subject to
--
--   - `hr`: $\mathrm{res}$ is a retraction of the structure map $\kappa_A \to \kappa(V)$;
--
--   - `hs`: for $a \in A_0$, the image in $\Omega$ of $\rho$ applied to the image of $a$ in $C_j$ is the image of $\theta(\text{residue of } a)$ under $\kappa_A \to \Omega$;
--
--   - `hp`: for every $c \in C_j$, $\mathrm{res}$ of the residue of $\rho(c)$ equals $\theta(\psi(c))$;
--
--   - `ht`: the image of $\rho(\mathtt{jChartFin})$ in $\Omega$ is transcendental over $\kappa_A$;
--
--   there exists a $\kappa_A$-algebra homomorphism
--   $$\mathrm{emb} : \kappa_A\bigl(j(\mathsf q^{d}) : d \mid M'\bigr) = \mathtt{modularFunctionFieldFullC } \kappa_A\, M' \longrightarrow \Omega$$
--   with the following two properties.
--
--   First, for every $gf \in \mathbb Q((\mathsf q))$ belonging to `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose image in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in `R₀.integers` (`hgi`) and which is cusp-regular, i.e. for every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ the inequality $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(j(\mathsf q))$ implies $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}(gf)$, and such that $\mathrm{qExpand}_{k_0,\ell'}$ of the coefficientwise image of $gf$ lies in $K$ (`hgK`) and, as an element of $K$, lies in $C_j$ (`hgC`): the value of $\mathrm{emb}$ at the image of `R₀.residue` of $gf$ under the inclusion `modularFunctionFieldC κ_A M' ≤ modularFunctionFieldFullC κ_A M'` equals the image in $\Omega$ of $\rho$ applied to that element of $C_j$.
--
--   Second, for every nonzero $d$ dividing $M'$ such that $\mathrm{qExpand}_{k_0,\ell'}$ of the coefficientwise image of $\mathrm{qExpand}_{\mathbb Q,d}(j(\mathsf q))$ lies in $K$ and, as an element of $K$, lies in $C_j$: $\mathrm{emb}$ sends `jqNFull κ_A M' d hd`, the element $j(\mathsf q^{d})$ of `modularFunctionFieldFullC κ_A M'`, to the image in $\Omega$ of $\rho$ applied to that element of $C_j$.
--
--   This is the step that converts a reading of modular functions along a branch of the special fibre — given by a homomorphism $\rho$ from the $j$-finite chart algebra of the integral model into the valuation ring of a place $V$ of $\Omega$, with $\rho(j)$ transcendental over $\kappa_A$ — into an embedding of the full level-$M'$ modular function field in characteristic $q$ into $\Omega$, pinned on the generators $j(\mathsf q^{d})$, $d \mid M'$, and on all $R_0$-integral cusp-regular rational level-$M'$ functions. It feeds the construction of moduli places of the reduced modular curve used in the level-lowering part of the argument, and is cited by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_isModuliPlaceOf_map_frobenius_of_forall_evalAt_eq_of_eq_map_classify_rigidDataPow_of_tatePoint`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_isModuliPlaceOf_map_frobenius_of_forall_evalAt_eq_of_eq_map_classify_rigidDataPow_of_tatePoint).
